1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:05:17,639
Mira: It feels like déjà vu. We've talked about sách in this coffee shop before, haven't we?

2
00:05:17,689 --> 00:10:35,328
Michael: Really? I don't remember much... But speaking of sách, I just finished reading "Sapiens" by Yuval Noah Harari. Have you đọc any of his works?

3
00:10:35,378 --> 00:20:07,129
Mira: Hmm, I don't like đọc science sách. I prefer classical Russian novels. Dostoevsky is my favorite author. Have you đọc "Crime and Punishment"?

4
00:20:07,179 --> 00:32:49,514
Michael: I've tried to đọc it several times but never finished. Russian sách are too... deep and sad. I prefer đọc sách about travel and cultures of different countries. But maybe I should try Dostoevsky again. Can you recommend any of his sách that are easier to đọc?

5
00:32:49,564 --> 00:39:10,731
Mira: There are no "easy to đọc" ones. Russian literature requires deep thinking. But... if you really want to try, I could lend you my copy of "The Idiot." That was the first Dostoevsky sách I đọc.

6
00:39:10,781 --> 00:46:35,476
Michael: Thank you, I'll try to đọc it. If I have any questions about the sách, could I ask you? Perhaps we could discuss sách while having coffee...

